            "rationale": "The oldest-first allocation rule is in Tier 2 (`Accounts.allocate`, `Accounts.fineStatus`). Tier 3 `Views` then re-derives what 'paid in full' and 'unpaid' mean with its own predicates. It also works out which fines a payment settled by comparing the library before and after, which is a status derivation outside Tier 2. The predicates agree with the Tier 2 allocation and do not contradict it, so this is a 1.",
