            "rationale": "The waiver rule itself is in Tier 2 (`Waivers.waive`, `Accounts.payable`). However, the change edits the Tier 4 CLI borrow check so that the borrow-block decision (owed >= 5.00) is still made in presentation code and now takes waivers into account. Tier 3 `Views` also decides waived, settled and paid-in-part status with its own predicates. A domain decision made in Tier 4 and touched by this change puts it at 0.",
